# The National Archives of Australia's born-digital file format standards: the formats it
# names as low risk of becoming obsolete, mapped to PRONOM ids so they can be compared with
# a disc's formats.csv (research/plan.md, "formats against a preservation list").
#
# The page names formats and extensions, not versions or PRONOM ids; each Puid below was
# chosen by hand from PRONOM's records (Siegfried's copy of them), with PRONOM's own name
# above it. Where the page names a format with no version, every version is listed. A
# format PRONOM cannot name (a codec inside a container) has no Puid and says why in Note.
#
# The standard is for files created from its date of issue. Existing files are handed to
# the NAA as they are, and it assesses them: a file outside this list is a fact to record,
# not a fault.
#
# Extensions are the page's, less those that are media types (x-tiff, x-mpeg3).
#
# Not yet read by arv: reference data (issue #53), here to be checked before code uses it.

%rec: List
%mandatory: Id Title Source Read

Id: naa-born-digital
Title: National Archives of Australia: born-digital file format standards
Source: https://www.naa.gov.au/information-management/storing-and-preserving-information/preserving-information/born-digital-file-format-standards
Read: 2026-10-20
Pronom: Siegfried's PRONOM data, github.com/richardlehane/siegfried commit 7fb430b (2026-09-27)
Note: The page's own tables, by category; the order is the page's.

%rec: Format
%mandatory: Name Category
%allowed: Name Category Extensions Puid Note

